WEBVTT - Most Fascinating Stories - Episode 199: The Modern Presidency: From Obama to Biden and the Resilient Republic (2008–Present)

1
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.440
[Rebecca] Welcome to Most Fascinating Stories.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.640
[Rebecca] I'm Rebecca.

3
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:12.000
[Rebecca] Today we arrive at a monumental milestone, the grand finale of our 90-episode U.S.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.200
[Rebecca] President series.

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:25.200
[Rebecca] From George Washington's icy crossing of the Delaware in 1776 to the turbulent currents of 21st century governance, the American presidency has endured as the world's greatest democratic experiment.

6
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:31.680
[Rebecca] Here is George with the modern era: Obama, Trump, Biden, and the resilient republic.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:58.160
[George] Taking office in January 2009, with the economy shedding 750,000 jobs each month, Barack Obama signed the $787 billion American Recovery and Reinvestment Act and rescued the iconic American automotive industry from liquidation, initiating the longest uninterrupted streak of private sector job creation in American history.

8
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:17.840
[George] In March 2010, after a year of ferocious congressional combat, Obama achieved what presidents since Theodore Roosevelt had dreamed of, signing the Landmark Affordable Care Act, extending health insurance coverage to 30 million uninsured Americans and outlawing discrimination against pre-existing conditions.

9
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:41.520
[George] Despite intense political backlash and the emergence of the conservative Tea Party movement in the 2010 midterms, Obama maintained a steady, long-term strategic focus on modernization, renewable energy investment, and progressive social reform, famously lighting the White House in rainbow colors in 2015 when the Supreme Court legalized marriage equality nationwide.

10
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:51.680
[George] The passage of the Affordable Care Act established the fundamental principle that healthcare is a right for all citizens, protecting millions from catastrophic medical debt.

11
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:59.920
[George] The Affordable Care Act stood as a monumental testament to the power of persistent political will in overcoming entrenched corporate opposition.

12
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:08.760
[George] The healthcare reforms championed by Obama extended basic security and human dignity to tens of millions of hardworking American families.

13
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:16.440
[George] The healthcare expansion represented the culmination of a century-long struggle to provide medical security to every American citizen.

14
00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:32.280
[George] On Sunday evening, May 1, 2011, President Obama stepped into the White House Situation Room alongside Vice President Joe Biden, Secretary of State Hillary Clinton, and the Joint Chiefs of Staff to monitor Operation Neptune Spear.

15
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:42.040
[George] Flying through pitch-black skies in stealth Black Hawk helicopters, Navy SEAL Team 6 raided a fortified compound in Abbitabad, Pakistan.

16
00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:51.480
[George] In 38 minutes of precision action, the SEALs eliminated Al-Qaeda mastermind Osama bin Laden, the architect of the September 11 attacks.

17
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:57.000
[George] At 11.35 that night, Obama addressed the nation and the world from the East Room.

18
00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:13.320
[George] Tonight, I can report to the American people and to the world that the United States has conducted an operation that killed Osama bin Laden, the leader of Al-Qaeda, and a terrorist who's responsible for the murder of thousands of innocent men, women, and children.

19
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:19.320
[George] The successful mission brought deep catharsis and justice to millions of grieving American families.

20
00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:29.560
[George] The elimination of Osama bin Laden brought justice and closure to the American people, demonstrating the peerless valor and professionalism of the United States military.

21
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:38.440
[George] The daring raid in Pakistan closed an agonizing chapter of national trauma, demonstrating the unyielding resolve of the American Republic.

22
00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:47.440
[George] The mission in Abbitabad was a triumph of intelligence, military courage, and presidential resolve that brought long-delayed justice to the world.

23
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:55.440
[George] That nighttime mission in Abbatabad reaffirmed the unbending commitment of the United States to hold accountable those who strike its people.

24
00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:11.280
[George] One of the most poignant and transcendent moments of Obama's presidency occurred in June 2015 in Charleston, South Carolina, following the horrific white supremacist mass shooting at Emanuel African Methodist Episcopal Church that claimed nine innocent lives.

25
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:22.640
[George] Delivering the eulogy for Reverend Clemente Pinckney before thousands of mourners, Obama delivered an unforgettable meditation on grace, racial reconciliation, and the burden of history.

26
00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:37.920
[George] In the middle of his address, the president paused, bowed his head, and in a rich, unscripted baritone, began to sing the opening stanza of the classic Christian hymn, Amazing Grace, how sweet the sound that saved a wretch like me.

27
00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:44.240
[George] The entire church stood, joined their voices with their commander-in-chief, and sang together in tears.

28
00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:52.320
[George] It was a moment of pure spiritual leadership that captured Obama's unique ability to minister to a grieving nation in its darkest hours.

29
00:04:52.320 --> 00:05:01.920
[George] Singing Amazing Grace in Charleston showed a president whose moral leadership and spiritual depth could heal a wounded community in its hour of darkest tragedy.

30
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:10.560
[George] The moment in Charleston showcased the transformative power of spiritual grace and empathy in transcending hate and uniting a divided community.

31
00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:19.120
[George] The singing in Charleston was an unforgettable act of spiritual leadership that reminded the nation of the healing power of forgiveness and grace.

32
00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:27.760
[George] The eulogy in Charleston stood as an enduring monument of American presidential eloquence, healing a broken community through moral leadership.

33
00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:35.160
[George] In 2016, the American political landscape was struck by a seismic shockwave with the emergence of Donald J.

34
00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:35.880
[George] Trump.

35
00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:47.480
[George] A billionaire real estate developer, reality television star, and populist outsider from Queens, New York, Trump shattered every established rule of presidential politics.

36
00:05:47.480 --> 00:06:06.280
[George] Defeating sixteen seasoned Republican primary challengers with flamboyant rallies and unvarnished social media communication, Trump championed an unapologetic America first platform, securing the southern border, rebuilding domestic manufacturing, and challenging globalist trade agreements.

37
00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:30.760
[George] In November 2016, running against Democratic nominee Hillary Clinton, Trump pulled off one of the greatest electoral upsets in American history, winning traditional Democratic blue wall states like Pennsylvania, Michigan, and Wisconsin, capturing 304 electoral votes and winning the presidency as the first person ever elected without prior military or government service.

38
00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:41.400
[George] The 2016 election of Donald Trump shattered political precedent, giving voice to millions of working class citizens who felt ignored by established political elites.

39
00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:50.680
[George] The populist movement led by Donald Trump redefined political debate, placing national sovereignty and American workers at the center of the agenda.

40
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:59.480
[George] The election of Donald Trump demonstrated the vibrant, unpredictable vitality of a populist democracy where the voters are always sovereign.

41
00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:08.040
[George] The populist movement showed that in a true democracy, the voice of the working class cannot be dismissed by coastal political establishments.

42
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:16.480
[George] President Donald Trump governed with volcanic energy, transforming the federal judiciary and reshaping American economic policy.

43
00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:32.960
[George] He enacted the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017, slashing corporate tax rates to stimulate domestic investment, eliminated thousands of federal regulations, and renegotiated NAFTA into the United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement, USMCA.

44
00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:44.240
[George] In foreign policy, Trump broke decades of diplomatic orthodoxy, meeting North Korean leader Kim Jong-un in historic summits in Singapore and Hanoi, moving the U.S.

45
00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:55.760
[George] Embassy to Jerusalem and brokering the historic Abraham Accords, normalizing diplomatic relations between Israel, the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain, and Morocco.

46
00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:10.800
[George] Trump's most enduring domestic achievement was appointing three conservative Supreme Court justices, Neil Gorsuch, Brett Kavanaugh, and Amy Coney Barrett, and hundreds of federal appellate judges, cementing a conservative judicial majority.

47
00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:20.000
[George] Trump's appointments transformed the American judicial landscape, while his Abraham Accords established historic new pathways to peace in the Middle East.

48
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:28.720
[George] The historic Abraham Accords shattered conventional diplomatic assumptions, opening a new era of cooperation and prosperity in the Middle East.

49
00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:36.800
[George] The Abraham Accords opened historic new pathways for peaceful commerce, security, and mutual recognition across the Middle East.

50
00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:46.240
[George] The Abraham Accords proved that innovative, bold diplomacy could build real bridges of cooperation across ancient theological and national divides.

51
00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:54.400
[George] In 2020, amid the unprecedented global disruption of the COVID-19 pandemic, former Vice President Joseph R.

52
00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.520
[George] Biden J.R.

53
00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:03.000
[George] was elected the 46th President of the United States, winning 81 million votes, the most in American history.

54
00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:16.440
[George] Taking office in January 2021, after decades of distinguished service in the Senate and White House, Biden focused on national healing, vaccine distribution, and rebuilding the nation's core infrastructure.

55
00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:36.280
[George] Partnering with bipartisan congressional coalitions, Biden signed the landmark $1.2 trillion Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act, the CHIPS and Science Act to revitalize domestic semiconductor manufacturing, and reasserted Western democratic unity in support of Ukraine against Russian aggression.

56
00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:51.000
[George] The peaceful continuity of the presidency proved that despite fierce partisan polarization and intense media debate, the constitutional framework established in Philadelphia in 1787 remained resilient, adaptable, and strong.

57
00:09:51.000 --> 00:10:00.360
[George] Joe Biden's presidency focused on rebuilding the physical foundations of America and reasserting democratic alliances in an era of global conflict.

58
00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:09.240
[George] Joe Biden's infrastructure investments and steady defense of democratic values abroad demonstrated the enduring resilience of American leadership.

59
00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:17.880
[George] Joe Biden's focus on national healing, infrastructure, and democratic unity affirmed the timeless resilience of the constitutional order.

60
00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:27.720
[George] Biden's historic legislative investments in bridges, broadband, and clean water laid the foundation for decades of future American industrial growth.

61
00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:35.400
[George] As we conclude our 90-episode journey across the American presidency, we look back upon an astonishing human tapestry.

62
00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:50.880
[George] From George Washington's icy Delaware Crossing and Abraham Lincoln's Gettysburg consecration to the Roosevelt New Deal, Eisenhower's Interstate Highways, Kennedy's Moonshot, Reagan's Berlin Wall Challenge, and the diverse leaders of the modern era.

63
00:10:51.120 --> 00:11:04.400
[George] The presidency has never been an office of saints or monarchs, but an intensely human crucible where ordinary citizens, elevated by the sovereign will of the people, wrestle with the monumental destinies of a free continent.

64
00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:10.880
[George] The American experiment is an unfinished symphony, a perpetual striving toward a more perfect union.

65
00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:28.480
[George] As we bid farewell to the presidents and prepare to cross the threshold into the ancient biblical empires of antiquity, we carry with us the timeless lesson of 250 years of republican liberty, that government of the people, by the people, and for the people, shall not perish from the earth.

66
00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:38.640
[George] The two and a half century journey of the American presidency stands as a glorious testament to the enduring strength and resilience of a free, self-governing people.

67
00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:49.120
[George] Across 90 episodes and two and a half centuries, the American presidency has endured as a beacon of liberty, proving that a free people can govern themselves in peace.

68
00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:58.320
[George] Across two and a half centuries, the American presidency has stood as the living engine of a free republic, an unfinished symphony of human liberty.

69
00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:08.880
[George] Across 90 magnificent episodes, the story of the American presidency is the living proof that a free nation can continually renew its devotion to human dignity.

70
00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:17.760
[Rebecca] With episode 199, we bring to a triumphant close our monumental 90 episode chronicle of the presidents of the United States.

71
00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:28.000
[Rebecca] From the Founding fathers of 1776 to the leaders of the modern era, thank you for journeying with us through two and a half centuries of American courage, crisis, and triumph.

72
00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:34.680
[Rebecca] Next week, Most Fascinating Stories embarks upon an epic brand new saga, The Great Biblical Empires.

73
00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:41.960
[Rebecca] We begin with episode 200, Ancient Egypt Part 1, The Pharaohs, the Nile, and the Exodus.

74
00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:46.440
